rfc8200.txt, rfc5095.txt, rfc5722.txt, rfc6437.txt, rfc6946.txt, rfc7045.txt, rfc7112.txt, rfc8883.txt, rfc9098.txt
    The texts of RFC 8200 (Internet Protocol, Version 6), RFC 5095 (Deprecation of Type 0 Routing Headers),
    RFC 5722 (Handling of Overlapping IPv6 Fragments), RFC 6437 (IPv6 Flow Label Specification), RFC 6946
    (Processing of IPv6 "Atomic" Fragments), RFC 7045 (Transmission and Processing of IPv6 Extension Headers),
    RFC 7112 (Implications of Oversized IPv6 Header Chains), RFC 8883 (ICMPv6 Errors for Discarding Packets
    Due to Processing Limits) and RFC 9098 (Operational Implications of IPv6 Packets with Extension Headers),
    downloaded from https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/ on 2026-10-26.
    License: the IETF Trust's Legal Provisions Relating to IETF Documents.
    Used: the rules the tests check (header of RFC 8200 §3, extension headers and options of §4, fragments
    of §4.5, the pseudo-header of §8.1, and the updates of RFC 5095, RFC 5722, RFC 6946, RFC 7045 and
    RFC 7112).

The IPv6 packets of the Linux kernel (fragmented echoes, MLDv2 reports with Hop-by-Hop options, NDP) are in
../../ethernet/linux.txt (see ../../ethernet/SOURCE).
